cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "lean-runtime: run Lean 4 proofs from Python or standalone files"
authors:
  - family-names: "Radisic"
    given-names: "Alejandro"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-7612-1082"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alerad/lean-runtime"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "2.9.1"
date-released: "2026-08-15"
abstract: >-
  lean-runtime executes Lean 4 code from Python or single .lean files
  without per-machine Lake projects or Mathlib source builds. It resolves
  the exact Lean environment a file needs from a catalog of prebuilt,
  pinned environments (Mathlib and matching LeanCert releases), supports
  reproducible environment lockfiles, downloads only the compressed module
  frames in a source's transitive import closure, and returns structured
  results recording the toolchain and dependencies actually used.
keywords:
  - "Lean 4"
  - "theorem proving"
  - "formal verification"
  - "Python"
  - "reproducibility"
  - "package management"
